    VERDICT: REFUSED -- compensation does not beat its own sham (-0.0 and
    +0.3 SE, 3.0 required). Reward cannot install the loop either, so the
    self-audition direction is closed WHOLE and not by half. Node
    perturbation correlates its own perturbations with reward and never
    needs to hear the result, which is the structural reason.

  AGAINST THE ZERO-SHIFT NULL (its own machinery, no shift)
    shift150 - shift0  +0.023 +/- 0.005  (+4.3 SE)
    shift300 - shift0  +0.022 +/- 0.008  (+2.9 SE)
    deaf     - shift0  -0.002            (must be at the floor)

  THE PRIMARY -- COHERENT RESPONSE AT THE SHIFT FREQUENCY. A closed
  loop moves produced F1 AT the shift rate; max|r| over 700 lags does
  not require that and is a maximum over noise.
    shift150 - shift0  -0.77 Hz +/- 0.22  (-3.4 SE)
    shift300 - shift0  +0.01 Hz +/- 0.23  (+0.0 SE)

  --- the reading ---
  REFUSED -- no shifted arm produces a COHERENT response at the
  shift frequency (-3.4 and 0.0 SE, 3.0 required), and every phase lag
  is indistinguishable from the two nulls. There is no phase-locked
  compensation, so the creature does not use self-audition to control
  F1. That CLOSES the closed-loop direction and independently explains
  why v62's integrator drifts freely: nothing is watching it.
  (max|r| over lags DID rise, 4.3 and 2.9 SE -- that statistic is a
  maximum over noise and is why the primary was corrected.)
